 2026-11-28   : 6.10.1
              - 6.10.1 : Update readme for recent changes.

 2026-11-27   : 6.10.0, origin/master
              - **6.10.0**
                - New: kea-config.tmpfiles
                  sets permission on /etc/kea/*.{pw,user}
                - New config option : kea_conf_dir
                    - defaults to /etc/kea
                  Gives option to use /etc/kea/<domain>. For example using this together with a
                  systemd drop-in file that specify config for kea-dhcp4:
            
                    ExecStart=/usr/bin/kea-dhcp4 -c /etc/kea/<domain>/kea-dhcp4-primary.conf

 2026-11-27   : 6.9.0
              - **6.9.0**
                - kea-ctrl has been dropped in kea upstream (functionality is incorporated in kea-dhcp4).
                - Config: Now uses files for passwords - be sure to copy all the password files
                  kea-auth-primary.pw, kea-auth-backup.pw and kea-auth-standby.pw files to every server.
                - Config Changes
                    - socket_dir has been removed (no longer needed)
                    - auth_user - no longer per server, it now belongs in global_variables section.
                - Convenience: provide files needed to build kea-git.
                  The version in AUR is out of date, and we our systemd unit files are more up to date.
                - Switch logging to use systemd journal instead of /var/log/kea
                - auth_server_password peer passwords can be randomly generated if empty or -random-
                - kea now requires the control user to be in a file not in the config

 2026-10-08   : 6.6.4
              - 6.6.4 Readme update

 2026-10-08   : 6.6.3
              - 6.6.3 Documentation on `readthedocs <https://kea-config.readthedocs.io>`
